      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "> Note: DrahtBot will probably close this automatically because of its heuristics. I still think this is an important discussion to have, since any improvement in what agents produce helps both maintainers and contributors.\r\n\r\nNo strong opinion, but just for reference:\r\n\r\n* Last time someone tried to add this file, it was highly controversial, because it would overwrite a possible local unstaged file.\r\n* My take is that this will make it easier for drive-by contributors to violate the ai policy and make it harder to spot them. All communications (including the PR description) must be written by a human and no LLM prompting can replace that.\r\n* Conversely, this can make it harder to  run experiments, where someone just wants to implement a feature for themselves, locally. (This was already raised when the AI policy itself was added, but this change would make it worse)\r\n* Also, this is going to include idk ~5k tokens in every prompt, which by itself may degrade performance/alignment.\r\n\r\nFundamentally, the issue you are trying to solve may be better fixed at a higher level (like at the git hoster side). Regardless, any approach here will likely be highly controversial and tedious.",
